Life has been pretty busy lately. Tomorrow will be week 10 of training for the Lincoln Half Marathon. 

It has been a LONG time since I’ve been able to commit 💯 to training. My consistency has been 👌 thanks to @jacqui_meadors and I’ve worked through a couple of nagging injuries thanks to @kerkvlietmary 

Finally, I’m very thankful to @itschelseakoch  and #VioletRayKoch for the daily love and support. I’m not sure what race day will bring, but it’ll be great because of the journey to get there. 

#thesweatlife 
@lululemon Ambassador
@run605 Owner
@605privatecoaching Coach

Spent last week speaking and teaching frisbee to more than 1,000 kids at 4 elementary schools in Penticton thanks to the sponsorship of Midtown RV!

Midtown also is donating 30 frisbees to every school! Huge thanks to Jeff Redmond for the support to helping introduce and getting more kids and adults into frisbee!

It was quite the week since I got food poisoning Tuesday night and so when I wasn't teaching, I was sleeping. I did end up also running a throwing clinic for Penticton Ultimate and got to see my step sister which was a nice bonus!

Heading to NY soon for the in-person WFDF board meeting!

