Who knew that my personal journey to wellness would lead me here. I am elated, honored, astonished, and grateful for this opportunity. I am going to focus on the first picture in this post for a moment because this truly is the picture that allowed me to open my eyes and understand exactly what was happening and what it would lead to. I was asked to be a lululemon run ambassador, and with this came a photoshoot. I was nervous, extremely nervous, as I am not very photogenic. I was sent my pictures after the photoshoot and had a serious breakdown. I was in tears. I was not happy at all with my photo. It was not what I was expecting. You see, I was a victim of vanity. I was so caught up in how I looked that I did not realize what the photo had captured and stood for. My friend said it best. It captures exactly who I am and who I represent. My smile and energy are felt thru my photo. It represents my mother, my grandmother, and all the strong Latina women in my life and my community. For that, I AM SO PROUD! 
I hope to make you all proud and continue to inspire you to live healthy lives. Thank you to @kt_hoagie and @morusssell for this opportunity and for recognizing the passion that I have for inclusion in the community. Thank you to @lululemon for the platform to showcase diversity and inclusion. Thank you to ALL my friends who have supported me and stood by me while on this mission.
@yogagirly4life and @robbest8180, it's an honor to share this platform with you!  Thank you to my fiance who has been my rock since day one and has all the patience in the world. I will continue to inspire and bring our community together. I've been told it is what I do best! #lululemonambassador #latinasrun #latinosrun #917girl #ZoiLa #inclusion #diversity #runcommunity #migente #sisepuede #correr #orgullosa #pride @latinosrunphoenix
