Home sitting by the fire for a minute. What an amazing day. It was COLD 🥶. 6 degrees air temp (feels like -15). This was year one of my business @run605 hosting the St. Patrick’s Day running festivities here in Sioux Falls. I have always loved this holiday, our parade and the three races that start the fun. My team worked their butts off today to make these races happen. I’m so proud to have earned the opportunity to put this event on. 

I’m also proud of the things that happened at the store while I was out on course. Our friends from @empoweru_sd (presenting race sponsor), @lululemon (amazing brand support), @runsiouxfalls (awesome club) and @cookiejareatery (yummy food & Mom & Dad) had the store packed with folks making memories and enjoying the day. 

We can’t control the weather, but we can control our attitudes and gratitudes. This is a great running community and this event is so much fun. 

Sláinte 

