10 pounds up at the end of this bulk! I wanted to share this side by side for the lil lady out there who’s scared to pick up weights or go through a bulk with the rest of looking bulky or gaining weight. 

This is the heaviest scale weight I’ve been in my entire life. And that’s the number one reason why I discourage getting on the scale for any reason other than to adjust how much food you should be eating in a day. The scale just tells us an overall number, it doesn’t take into account what is fat and what is muscle. 

Did I gain some fat this bulk? Sure did. I think it’s pretty easy to spy in my stomach. But I can also see a positive change in my glutes and hamstrings, growth! I didn’t use bulking as an excuse to eat like crap, binge out, and work a little less hard. I fed my body how it needed to be fed, put my all into the gym and recovery, and prioritized protein. Going through a bulk doesn’t have to mean you’re going to put on mounds of fat!!! So to the girl who’s scared to get uncomfy…. DO IT. wear a big sweatshirt for a little while if it gets to your head. But seeing the growth is so rewarding and it’s the only way we’re going to grow. 

Ps: @ptulaactive northern lights collection dropped this weekend. Check it out! 

