Have you noticed less supersets in my lega day recently? I’ve made this little change and increased the rep range I was using to the 12-15 range instead, really making sure I’m focusing on tempo each rep. Why 12-15? Our legs are composed of a lot of muscles. The quads, used in this workout, are made up of four muscles (vs let’s say the biceps which have two). The bigger the muscle group the more it can handle. 

With all that said, let’s dive into the workout: 

1️⃣ back squat 5x5
2️⃣ pendulum squat (mod with hack or goblet squat) 4x12 
3️⃣step ups 4x12 
4️⃣lateral lunges 4x12
5️⃣spanish squats 4x15

