LOCKED IN. 

Race day has become the new game day for me. I love the feelings I get. The nervousness. The fear. The anxiety. It builds up so much that I can barely contain myself. Then the switch flips. 

The calmness takes over the storm. My emotions turn into excitement and darkness. Everything is silent for a moment. I’m free. Ready for war. 

I love that feeling, I live for that feeling. I thought I’d never get that feeling again. And then I found racing. When I toe the line of an event I am ready to leave everything on the course. I truly am at peace. 

Racing is such a singular sport where everything is on you. All your preparation and training is put to the test. There is nowhere to hide, there are no excuses. It doesn’t matter how good you did in training if you can’t throw it together on race day. It’s examination day. I love that pressure and I love the opportunity to #proveyourselfright and test the limits of the mind and body. 

Although it’s a singular sport; you vs. You, I love racing. I love competing and pushing to one day “break the tape” and win a race. My time will come. For now I’m locked in and ready to go to war with myself and anyone else on the course. 

Keep going. 

