Grateful. 

I am grateful for what I’ve been through. I am grateful for my past. Everything that has ever happened to me. Things that I once thought defined me, things that I thought I couldn’t escape from; I’m grateful for it all. I am grateful for the body I have been blessed with and the body I have built. I am grateful for what it is capable of and what it will be able to do in the future. For too long I abused it. Hated it and mistreated it. I used to hate the way I looked. Now it a vessel of work. Built for performance and maintained for longevity. 

When you become friends with the dark you learn to live with the pain and keep going. 

Life isn’t fair. It sucks at points, but there is always growth on the other side of pain. 

I found purpose in the struggle. Through my failures and coming short I found the love of my life. I found my family and true friends. I found my tribe and my life’s work. I have proved to myself time and time again that I can do anything. My story has a purpose and I will not shy away from it any more. If me sharing my experiences helps even one person to keep going and to not give up then I’ve done my job. 

I will never quit, and I will never let you quit either. 

Keep going. #OMT 

