@lululemon is the latest brand that @nike has sued over “infringement” of their products. Nike has made a lawsuit against Lululemon claiming that Lululemon stole its Flyknit designs. Nike specifically called out four different shoes that use similar materials the Chargefeel Mid, Chargefeel Low, Blissfeel, and Strongfeel shoes. Nike made a statement saying the company has “suffered economic harm and irreparable injury” from Lululemon infringing its patented material. 

Lululemon spokesperson said that “Nike’s claims are unjustified, and we look forward to proving our case in court.”

This isn’t the first time Nike has taken legal action against Lululemon either. Last year, they sued Lululemon for infringing on its Mirror home gym technology.

