Something I wish I had learned a lilll earlier in life: your hamstrings have an affect on your lower back. Yep. The tightness of your hamstrings could be causing pain in your lower back. So if you’re engaging your core, your form is spot on, and you’re still wondering why you feel some pain, this might be why. Tight hamstrings pull on the pubic bone which makes the back arch back, causing the pain. That’s my little fun fact today. 

On a lighter note, here’s a hammy n glute workout. Make sure y’all stretch after!!! 

1️⃣sumo deadlift 5x5
2️⃣bb RDL 4x10
3️⃣wide stance leg press 4x10 into 10 calf raises 
SUPERSET 4 and 5
4️⃣db stiff leg deadlift 4x10
5️⃣SL db hip thrust 4x10
6️⃣abductions 4x10 full into 10 pulsing 

Bookmark this!! Sign up for 1:1 training with me and we’ll work on those hammies together. 

