SUFFERING IS HEALING. 

I have always been determined and stubborn. But I wasn’t always the person you all see today. The reason I am so open about my struggles and my past is because I know it can help just one person out there to see that their life is worth it and they can to change their life. It also helps me to heal my own traumas and strengthen the bond I have with suffering and progress. 

Learning to suffer willingly and deal with emotions and work at it daily has given me some of the best and worst days of my life. I truly believe that suffering is necessary to progress but you have to realize nobody can save you from your past. You can however understand that it’s not your fault. You are not your past and you absolutely do have a future if you choose to go through the dark and put the work in on yourself physically and mentally. 

If I can be a lesson to anyone it’s to never give up. I have gone through a lot and I have survived and become stronger. I also understand and know that I have been through NOTHING compared to others in this life. I hope they can too become stronger from their pain and bring light to those who are still scared in the dark. 

Mental health and struggle is something I feel passionate about because I’ve seen, experienced and personally been through some of the things it can cause. It’s okay to not to be okay but it isn’t okay to give up. 

Your life is worth it and the world is a better place with all of us in it. 

This year we #proveyourselfright but it starts by having the will to #changeyourmindchangeyourlife 

Keep going. #OMT 

