It’s a gift to see this town come together for a good cause. 

@sweatsafetucson was an initiative to provide a service that often times prices people out, or that they may not initially see the value in. The form in which this often presents itself is health, and how we invest in ourselves. So we granted 20 gym memberships to a deserving group of individuals, and dispersed the memberships across town. We wanted to guide people into Safe spaces, for them to train, learn, and be vulnerable. These are the leaders in our community that we trusted with such a task.

When I was younger, people in this very group influenced me to make a change in my life, and it’s made all the difference. If this program helped just one person, then we reached our desired goal. I’m convinced it did more than that. 

Seeing all these leaders of health, and fitness in one room has been gift enough this holiday season. Thank you all for being the leaders you are, creating safe spaces, and being a beacon for health & wellness.❤️

