Training has been fun, I’m not gonna lie, & it’s been very “doable”… 😀

If you’re constantly failing yourself and not showing up, try to make the goal, AND the PROCESS of achieving it a little bit more desirable 

If you can’t show up 5 days a week to the gym, then don’t set that as a goal. Start with what you know you can.. maybe 3 days? Start there, have fun, and you’ll be surprised to see how you start to shift things in your life to make more time for the things that are important to you 
♥️

Honestly, my life feels like a tornado right now but I’m just riding a cow flying around in it. And it’s kind of fun. 

I’ve talked about this before but “staying afloat” is part of life, so make sure you’re living it. We often think of hitting our goals or doing fun things as “life” and then toss the rest in the garbage. 

Workout, sleep, go to work, see some friends, read a book, build something, color, go for a run, learn something new, stare at the wall. It’s all life. Don’t worry 😉 

