This picture means a lot to me. It shows me broken, beat up, physically shattered and mentally tired. 

To be honest I was disappointed after this task. I didn’t accomplish the goal fully. I wanted to run the 100km sub 15 hours with a goal of 13hrs; it took me 16. 

I had put in the work. I had prepared with the time I had to work with and I was ready. But I made mistakes I have continuously made before: messing up my nutrition. This killed me (almost literally) and significantly slowed me down and forced me to walk and even pass out at one point. 

What this photo also shows me is the amount of battling I did that day and throughout the journey leading up to the 100km ultra. 

Not only did I physically battle everyday I mentally battled to stay disciplined on track and focused. I stayed the course and battled to get everything out myself that day too. What was happening in this picture was the revelation I search for during these journeys; 

I had really forgotten the bigger picture. We just raised $6000 for the youth in Barrie, I fricken ran all night 105km for 16hrs from Barrie to the @cntower . I grew so much as a person and as a community supporter / youth mentor. I found myself once again becoming grateful for my losses and my triumphs. Now there is no losing, only learning. Keep going. 

Thanks for capturing this @deanheliotis I can’t wait for 2023 😈👀 

