We can’t fit all the success of yesterday in one post, so be prepared for multiple! 😅 

Yesterday was the second of our annual “The Weight of War” event built by @joshjatkins.  This is what the voice of just one man can do, resonate in the hearts of many, and go on to truly change and save lives. When you’re selfless, people show up, selflessly. Thank you all. 

What was most memorable for us other than the epic effort from all who ran 🏃‍♂️ 🏃‍♀️ 🏃 was the dialogue people opened up with at the support party, either about themselves or a sister or brother they knew who needed us. Memories made and lives changed, this is what it’s all about. 

Last years first annual event began with one man, a couple of mates, and a small support party, take a look at these pics to see how that seed has grown. Thank you all. ❤️ 

Yesterday began with a community of people connecting with with big smiles and laughs while fighting one common cause, the veteran suicide epidemic in which we have a scalable solution (click link in our bio). 

We will add up the sales of t-shirts, over 1000 raffle tickets sold, the karma kegs from the party and your contributions today, but we are certain Josh has smashed through his 10k goal to sponsor 10 veterans on the STTN program. 👏  You can still contribute by clicking the link in Josh’s bio or going to: https://survivetothrivenation.com/weight-of-war/

We want to do a special shout out to @runarmyau. What a truly special cause. You are all incredible thank you for showing up in big numbers!

@felonsbrewingco for the sponsorship fundraiser and epic event - everyone had a blast!

@budgysmuggler for making peeps look dead sexy 🔥 

@lululemonausnz - for your raffle, setting up your stand, and fighting the good fight with us! ❤️ 

@thepineappleexpress_vc - thank you for your post sharing and support of our cause 🍍 ❤️ 

And of course, Josh. Stand proud. 🇦🇺 

