DON’T SHY AWAY FROM PRESSURE! 

I post on social media as an outlet for me to express myself. For me to be me and showcase how far I have come and where I’m going to go. It’s a journal of my journey. I also post on here to help motivate, inspire, and push people to become the best versions of themselves and try and be better everyday. 

With that comes pressure. Sure most of it is perceived because for the most part most of you don’t care at all about what I’m doing and the goals I’m hunting. But, for the few of who do care, and whom I do help to motivate and push to do something and get uncomfortable; telling y’all and showing y’all everything I’m doing and want to do adds pressure. 

A lot of us run from pressure. I do not and will not run from it. Announcing that I’ll be hunting the elusive sub 3 hour marathon adds pressure. The doubters perch up, the negative thoughts creep in and the anxiety of possibly not achieving the goal while telling everyone online that I’m going to, becomes daunting. 

I have learned to love the pressure. I love the doubt, the unknown and the fear of failure. It pushes me to be even better and push the limits even more. 

This 16 week prep is going to be gruelling. It’s going to be repetitive, boring at times and lonely. But this is the path I’ve chosen and this is the goal I’m hunting. 

Do not be afraid of the pressure. Remember, pressure creates diamonds. Learn to thrive in it. 

Keep going. #OMT 

@austinmarathon I’m coming for you. And I’m smashing sub 3 hours. 
